\begin{abstract}
This Codex defines the complete optical physics, engineering tolerances,
phase-control algorithms, and reconstruction fidelity requirements for the
ENERGIZE Precision Reconstruction Laser System. The reconstruction laser array
performs atomic-scale deposition using sub-picosecond pulses, synchronized to
astrophysical QKD entropy keys to ensure perfect atomic restoration with
fidelity $\mathcal{F} \ge 0.999999$.
\end{abstract}

% ============================================================
\section{System Overview}
% ============================================================

The Reconstruction Laser System integrates:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Ti:Sapphire mode-locked femtosecond lasers,
    \item Zero-expansion optical benches,
    \item Cryogenic SNSPD phase-feedback loops,
    \item QKD-synchronized phase-control algorithms,
    \item Sub-nanometer atomic deposition actuators.
\end{itemize}

The system reconstructs atomic lattices using Q-LDPC-corrected state tensors
and astrophysical entropy keys $H_{\text{astro}}$.

% ============================================================
\section{Laser Physics \& Pulse Structure}
% ============================================================

\subsection{Pulse Generation}

The reconstruction laser emits pulses with:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Center frequency: $438\ \mathrm{THz}$,
    \item Pulse width: $<120\ \mathrm{fs}$,
    \item Spectral bandwidth: $>8\ \mathrm{nm}$,
    \item Repetition rate: $80\ \mathrm{MHz}$.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Phase-Control Equation}

Atomic reconstruction requires phase alignment between the incoming encrypted
tensor $\mathbf{E}_{\text{stream}}$ and the deposition pulse:

\[
\phi_{\text{laser}}(t) = \phi_{\text{QKD}}(t) + \Delta\phi_{\text{LDPC}}(t)
\]

where:

\begin{itemize}
    \item $\phi_{\text{QKD}}(t)$ is derived from $H_{\text{astro}}$,
    \item $\Delta\phi_{\text{LDPC}}(t)$ corrects parity block offsets.
\end{itemize}

% ============================================================
\section{Optical Bench \& Alignment Requirements}
% ============================================================

\subsection{Bench Requirements}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Zero-expansion composite material,
    \item Thermal drift $<0.1\ \mu\mathrm{m}$,
    \item Vibration isolation: $<0.5\ \mathrm{nm}$ RMS.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Alignment Tolerances}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Beam pointing stability: $<0.5\ \mu\mathrm{rad}$,
    \item Path delay mismatch: $<0.001\ \mathrm{nm}$,
    \item Fiber coupling loss: $<0.3\ \mathrm{dB}$.
\end{itemize}

% ============================================================
\section{QKD-Synchronized Reconstruction Loop}
% ============================================================

\subsection{Entropy-Locked Phase Synchronization}

The reconstruction loop uses astrophysical entropy keys:

\[
H_{\text{astro}} = \mathrm{SHA3\text{-}512}(\text{Pulsar} + \text{CMB})
\]

to generate phase masks:

\[
M_{\phi} = H_{\text{astro}} \oplus \mathbf{S}_{\text{tensor}}
\]

\subsection{Real-Time Feedback}

SNSPD detectors provide:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Timing jitter: $<12.4\ \mathrm{ps}$,
    \item Phase error feedback at $80\ \mathrm{MHz}$,
    \item Decoherence monitoring via QBER.
\end{itemize}

% ============================================================
\section{Atomic Deposition Mechanics}
% ============================================================

\subsection{Deposition Actuator Requirements}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Sub-nanometer positioning resolution ($<0.001\ \mathrm{nm}$),
    \item Piezoelectric actuator bandwidth: $>500\ \mathrm{kHz}$,
    \item Thermal drift compensation: active.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Reconstruction Fidelity}

Atomic reconstruction fidelity is computed as:

\[
\mathcal{F} = \left( \mathrm{Tr}\sqrt{\sqrt{\rho_{\text{in}}}\rho_{\text{out}}
\sqrt{\rho_{\text{in}}}} \right)^2
\]

ENERGIZE requires:

\[
\mathcal{F} \ge 0.999999
\]

